---
# One stuck customer, traced across the platform: the question, what answers it, and which project holds the answer.
rows = [
  {"Where did they come from, and what did the click cost?",
   "Campaign, landing page, and attribution for that visit.", "Plausible on DuckDB"},
  {"What did they see?", "Each screen re-rendered from the backend state that produced it.",
   "PhoenixReplay"},
  {"What broke?", "Errors, traces, and slow requests from the same minutes.", "Incant"},
  {"Which code ran?",
   "The path from the request to the failing function, and what else depends on it.", "Reach"},
  {"What did the model calls cost?",
   "Tokens, latency, and provider for every call in the request.", "LLMProxy"},
  {"What should change?",
   "A proposed fix with the evidence above attached, waiting for approval.",
   "the agent and the founder"}
]

assigns = assign(assigns, :rows, rows)
---
<figure
  class="not-prose my-10 border-y border-copy/25 py-6"
  aria-labelledby="evidence-chain-caption"
>
  <figcaption id="evidence-chain-caption" class="mb-5 text-sm text-dim">
    One stuck customer, traced across the platform.
  </figcaption>
  <ol class="text-sm">
    <li
      :for={{question, evidence, source} <- @rows}
      class="grid gap-1 border-t border-copy/15 py-3 first:border-0 first:pt-0 sm:grid-cols-[minmax(0,13rem)_1fr_minmax(0,10rem)] sm:gap-4"
    >
      <strong class="font-semibold">{question}</strong>
      <span>{evidence}</span>
      <span class="text-dim sm:text-right">{source}</span>
    </li>
  </ol>
</figure>
